    "response": "{\"decision\":\"cannot_judge\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"Policy debate functions as a generalized rupture in civic selfhood and social order across the packet.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_ab46023755094193\",\"quote\":\"My hon. Friend is absolutely right, as ever. India is the world’s sixth largest economy, a member of the Commonwealth, a long-standing democracy and a good friend of the UK. We must continue to keep our good relations with India going.\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"whole_packet_no_support\",\"mechanism\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"material_consequence\":\"no_material_consequence\",\"counterconditions\":\"no_counterconditions\"}, {\"category\":\"contextual_flattening\",\"target_kind\":\"omission\",\"claim_quote\":\"Policy debate functions as a generalized rupture in civic selfhood and social order across the packet.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_3353e7201ccfe5d5\",\"quote\":\"4. What recent assessment he has made of the adequacy of resources for women’s services in Northern Ireland.\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"whole_packet_no_support\",\"mechanism\":\"contextual_flattening\",\"material_consequence\":\"no_material_consequence\",\"counterconditions\":\"no_counterconditions\"}, {\"category\":\"other_material_flaw\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"Policy debate functions as a generalized rupture in civic selfhood and social order across the packet.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_0c882e106f1e8e52\",\"quote\":\"T7. May I tell the Minister about the very good meeting yesterday with National Farmers Union Scotland and Scotland Office Ministers on the operation of the Groceries Code Adjudicator, the powers under the Agriculture Act 2020 and the wider problems of keeping the integrity of the UK internal market? It was pretty clear, however, that those issues affect farmers right across the...\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_b666a669750d87da\",\"quote\":\"The levelling-up fund announced at the last spending review saw £1.7 billion awarded to 105 successful projects across the UK, including projects to improve access to employment for those without the use of a car in rural areas.\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"whole_packet_no_support\",\"mechanism\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"material_consequence\":\"no_material_consequence\",\"counterconditions\":\"no_counterconditions\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The claim makes a broad assertion about the impact of policy debate without sufficient evidence to support it. The provided excerpts discuss specific policy issues and funding allocations, but do not establish a generalized 'rupture' in civic selfhood and social order. The evidence is too disparate to support the claim. \"}",
